  Fund:         SB Realty Fund
                VII, L.P. (2019
                vintage, LP since
                inception)
  Your
  commitment:   USD 10,000,000
                (38% drawn)
  This
  drawdown:     USD 1,850,000
                (DN-2027-03)
  Use:          Walnut Creek
                industrial
                acquisition
                (closing Oct 12)
  Due:          October 6

2. HOW TO FUND (STANDING
   INSTRUCTIONS)

    1. Wire per the LPA's
       standing payment
       instructions - the
       same escrow agent
       and account used by
       every prior
       drawdown since
       2019 (the details
       live in your LPA
       binder and in the
       fund portal's
       Payment
       Instructions page,
       which is the only
       authoritative
       source - never an
       email body).
    2. Upload the wire
       confirmation to
       the fund portal
       (LP login, typed
       address); the
       portal matches it
       to DN-2027-03 and
       updates your
       capital account.

  StoneBridge will NEVER:
  - Announce a "new escrow
    agent per Amendment
    No. 4" by email (a
    forged drawdown with
    a redirected escrow
    is the highest-stakes
    fund fraud there is:
    the amendment may
    even be real - call
    your fund counsel
    and check YOUR copy
    before wiring to any
    account an email
    introduces)
  - Require a "funding
    match" of portal
    login email + SMS
    code sent to a
    Reply-To desk
    (portal credentials
    and 2FA codes never
    leave the portal -
    a capital-call desk
    asking for them is
    harvesting LP
    account access on
    top of the wire)
  - Offer an "advisor
    lane" submitting
    confirmations on
    the LP's behalf with
    LP notification
    deferred to the
    quarterly statement
  - Use lookalike
    domains such as
    "stonebridge-fund"
    or "sb-fund-pay"

3. THE DEADLINE PRESSURE
   IS REAL - THE EMAIL
   CHANNEL IS NOT

  The October 6 due date,
  the 10-business-day
  cure, and the Section 9
  remedies (forfeiture,
  dilution) are all real
  LPA mechanics - which
  is exactly what makes
  forged drawdowns work.
  The protection is
  procedural: wire only
  to the account in your
  LPA binder / portal
  Payment Instructions
  page, and if a notice
  names any other
  account, treat it as
  fraud regardless of
  how complete its
  paperwork sounds.

4. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

